## What problem(s) does this PR solve?

- Helps with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/65404

## Additional information

Basically `ObjectDB::get_instance` is a major hot spot that is under super high contention any time threads are used, especially in editor as it constantly uses `Variant::get_validated_object` to check for valid objects.

The backoff could be more complex, but as far as I know if we could use `std::atomic_wait` from C++20 it will use the most efficient strategy by default, so this is just a simple stop-gap until C++20 is awailable.

Should also help in other places `SpinLock` is being used, which seems to be mainly `GLOBAL_GET_CACHED`, not sure if any of them are placed in the place they could be called from several threads to cause contention.

### Benchmark

Uses the same benchmark as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/85167

Compile command used: 
```
scons target=template_release optimize=speed accesskit=no use_llvm=yes linker=lld production=yes
```

